Changes from upstream 0.18.2
----------------------------

1. Renamed to @phi/ui and repointed at Phi Lab's internal registry.

2. Bundled typefaces removed. Upstream shipped Collapse, Mondwest, Neuebit
   and Rules (Compressed/Expanded) as .woff2 files. Those are commercial
   typefaces from their respective foundries; the package's MIT licence
   covers its own source, not the right to redistribute third-party font
   binaries. This fork therefore ships no font files.

   The --font-* CSS variable contract is unchanged, so consumers need no code
   changes. src/styles/fonts.css now points those variables at the Phi visual
   identity, all open-licensed for commercial use:

       --font-sans     Figtree
       --font-display  Spectral
       --font-mono     DM Mono

   The legacy aliases (--font-rules-compressed, --font-rules-expanded,
   --font-mondwest, --font-neuebit) are kept as pointers to the above so that
   existing class names keep resolving instead of silently falling back to a
   system stack. Anyone holding a licence for the original typefaces can
   register their own @font-face rules against the same variables.

3. NousGirlBadge removed — an illustrated Nous mascot, not ours to ship.

4. Storybook, MSW, Playwright and Vitest dev-dependencies dropped; this fork
   is consumed as a library and does not build the story catalogue. The
   peer-dependency type sources (three, gsap, leva, motion, plot) are kept
   because src imports them in 11 places.

Component APIs are deliberately untouched, so the 46 call sites in the Phi
Agent dashboard needed no changes.

